  "review": [
    {
      "@type": "Review",
      "reviewRating": {
        "@type": "Rating",
        "ratingValue": "5"
      },
      "author": {
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": "Zach G"
      },
      "reviewBody": "I started making this for a couple of years (first using another recipe then this one) as a frequent weeknight meal for me and my wife - we both love it. I know this is probably sacrilege, but the last two times (including tonight), I added some sliced mushrooms while saut\u00e9ing the guanciale. It adds another flavorful and filling layer to the dish."
    },
    {
      "@type": "Review",
      "reviewRating": {
        "@type": "Rating",
        "ratingValue": "5"
      },
      "author": {
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": "Chris Long"
      },
      "reviewBody": "Pretty much perfect. There is no question that using both guanciale and pecorino is a requirement to make this dish perfect and true to its roots. I used a full pound of rigatoni, and needed around 3 cups of pasta water in total"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Review",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": "Daniel Pepper"
      },
      "reviewBody": "Delicious. We made it for the third time tonight. We use slightly less guanciale (in gms) per serving, and next time will add at least 50% more of the starch water to the fat at the get-go, since we seemed to use more than double the called for starch water to get our Rusticelli Penne Rigati to the point where the chalky white disappears. But, yummy! Could close our eyes and taste Rome. Thank you so much"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Review",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": "Northern Gabagool"
      },
      "reviewBody": "I've made this twice now, once with slab bacon, and once with guanciale. While the dish with bacon was good, the dish with guanciale was so much better. It's definitely worth tracking some down!"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Review",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": "goodtherapy"
      },
      "reviewBody": "During a road trip, and with pots and pans less than ideally suited to the task, I used a mix of pancetta and cubed prosciutto, and the result was...transporting. This is a terrific, and obviously easily adapted, recipe"
    }
  ],
